t quarter.\n- I found no figures for 2026 or for years beyond 2027.\n\n**Policy path (a mild risk).**\n- The CMA held at 4.50% in October. Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut in 2027.\n- Futures price a 25bp cut in 2027Q2 and a second one in 2027Q4, so about 50bp in total. That is twice the CMA's base case. Ashby said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves\".\n\n**Valuation.**\n- The weighted forward P/E is 19x.\n- The holdings are long-duration growth names. Historically, a 50bp lower policy path has lifted the basket P/E by about 1.5 points.\n- The market already prices the 50bp of easing, so the 19x multiple likely includes that lift.\n- If the CMA delivers only its one cut, the multiple could lose about 0.75 points (roughly 4%). That is my estimate, assuming the sensitivity scales linearly.\n- A 14% EPS gain more than offsets that. With a flat multiple, price should rise roughly in line with EPS. With the multiple at about 18.25x, the net is still roughly +9–10%.\n\n**Caveats.**\n- The case is sensitive to the pace of easing, not its direction. The risk would be a hawkish repricing late in 2027.\n- The top five holdings are 49% of the fund, so a miss at Voltaris (14%) or Tarnwell (11%) on backlog conversion would hurt most.\n- The sources give no CMA meeting calendar.\n- I did not check options-implied or realized volatility (the `vltx_iv` and `vltx_rv` series).\n\nDetail is in n4.r1 (policy path) and n5.r1 (holdings).","ttft_ms":2859,"type":"result","duration_ms":55703,"uuid":"a99326f6-997a-4832-a40b-9718b3733d04","ttft_stream_ms":1158,"time_to_request_ms":122,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":36,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":16,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool